"cli.help.nativepiperemoteapp.cli" = "Usage: nativepipe [options] user@host application [arguments...]\n\nWaypipe for macOS: run Linux apps over SSH in native Mac windows.\nSSH handles authentication and communication without port forwarding.\n\n  nativepipe --install-compositor user@host gtk4-demo\n  nativepipe user@host firefox --no-remote\n  nativepipe -p 2222 -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 user@host qterminal\n\nConnect and launch (options before user@host):\n  --compositor PATH      Remote executable (default: nativepipe-wayland)\n                         A custom path bypasses automatic installation\n  --install-compositor   Install/update compositor from GitHub Release\n  -i FILE, -F FILE, -J HOST, -p PORT, -o OPTION, -4, -6, -A, -a\n                         Pass an authentication/connection option to SSH\n  --no-progress          Hide terminal connection status (diagnostics remain)\n  -h, --help             Show local help without connecting/installing\n\nThe Linux application must already be installed. --install-compositor installs\nonly the NativePipe compositor, as your SSH user, without root access.\nAfter the destination, all arguments (including --help) belong to the Linux app.\nKeep the app in the foreground: its exit ends the session.\n\nAutomate:\n  nativepipe -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 user@host gtk4-demo 2>session.log\n  nativepipe --help\n  nativepipe --version\n\nOutput: stdout stays empty; SSH/compositor/application diagnostics go to stderr.\nTerminal stderr also shows connection stages; redirected stderr has no UI\nprogress or color. No percentage is invented. Exit 2 means invalid CLI input;\notherwise the SSH/session status is preserved (255 commonly means SSH failed).\n130 means sign-in was cancelled or Ctrl-C was pressed.\nCtrl-C or the app's Disconnect menu ends this session. Sessions have no durable\ntask ID or resume/query API; a new invocation starts a new Linux command.\nUse BatchMode=yes for unattended SSH without authentication dialogs.\nRelated: ssh for login diagnostics; --install-compositor for compositor updates.\nGuide: https://github.com/shih-liang/NativePipe#usage";
"dbus-run-session is required to run applications in their own session. Install dbus-daemon (Debian/Ubuntu) or dbus (Arch/Alpine), and check PATH." = "dbus-run-session is required to run applications in their own session. Install dbus-daemon (Debian/Ubuntu) or dbus (Arch/Alpine), and check PATH.";
